 "captions": {
  "script": "This tree bleeds when you cut it. Glitch Diary, entry three. Socotra, an island off Yemen, cut off from Arabia for millions of years. Here grow dragon's blood trees, shaped like umbrellas turned inside out. Cut the bark, and the sap hardens into a dark red resin. But that's not the strange part. The umbrella is a machine. Its dense crown catches fog, dew and rain, and sends the water down to its roots. And there's something even stranger. More than a third of Socotra's plants grow nowhere else on Earth. Some of these trees may be over seven hundred years old. Would you walk through this alien forest? Comment below. Follow for the next entry of my glitch diary. Because this tree...",
